#!/bin/sh
# iwato-desktop-doctor: what to look at when the desktop does not start
# (Xvfb "Failed to compile keymap" and the like). Prints facts; changes nothing
# except a short Xvfb test run on display :97 in a temp directory.
echo "== id and directories"; id
ls -ld /tmp /tmp/.X11-unix /var/lib/xkb 2>&1
echo "== programs"
command -v Xvfb xkbcomp selkies-session 2>&1
xkbcomp -version 2>&1 | head -n 1
echo "== seccomp / capabilities"
grep -E '^(NoNewPrivs|Seccomp|CapEff)' /proc/self/status
# Xvfb's xkbcomp child calls setgid(getgid()) and setuid(getuid()) and exits
# 127 when either fails: under the sandbox's seccomp filter they do.
python3 -c '
import os
for f, a in ((os.setgid, os.getgid()), (os.setuid, os.getuid())):
    try: f(a); print(f.__name__ + "(own id): ok")
    except OSError as e: print(f.__name__ + "(own id): " + str(e) + "  <- Xvfb cannot start xkbcomp without the shim")
' 2>&1
echo "== shim"
ls -l /usr/local/lib/iwato/libiwato-noid.so 2>&1
echo "LD_PRELOAD=${LD_PRELOAD:-}"
echo "== Xvfb :97 for 5 seconds (with LD_PRELOAD as the shell has it)"
d="$(mktemp -d)" && cd "$d" || exit 1
if timeout 5 Xvfb :97 >"$d/xvfb.out" 2>&1; then :; else rc=$?; [ "$rc" = 124 ] && echo "Xvfb stayed up (OK)" || { echo "Xvfb exited with $rc:"; tail -n 20 "$d/xvfb.out"; }; fi
rm -rf "$d" /tmp/.X97-lock /tmp/.X11-unix/X97 /tmp/server-97.xkm 2>/dev/null
echo "== browser (what a link click uses)"
echo "BROWSER=${BROWSER:-}  IWATO_DESKTOP_SESSION=${IWATO_DESKTOP_SESSION:-}"
command -v firefox x-www-browser sensible-browser xdg-open exo-open xfce4-mime-helper 2>&1
readlink -f /usr/bin/x-www-browser 2>&1
grep -H WebBrowser ~/.config/xfce4/helpers.rc /etc/xdg/xfce4/helpers.rc 2>&1
grep -H -E 'x-scheme-handler/https?=|text/html=' ~/.config/mimeapps.list /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list 2>&1
xdg-mime query default x-scheme-handler/https 2>&1
xfce4-mime-helper --query WebBrowser 2>&1
timeout 20 firefox --version 2>&1 | head -n 2
echo "== log"; tail -n 20 "${IWATO_DESKTOP_LOG:-${HOME:-/sandbox}/.cache/iwato-desktop.log}" 2>&1
